      ":question/problem": "Prove by contradiction that $6\u2224(3n - 8)$ for any $n \u2208 Z$.\n\nAssume, for a contradiction, that $6$ {{field-1}} $(3n - 8)$. Then, {{field-2}}, where $k$ is an integer.\n\nTherefore, we have the following equivalence:\n\n$3n - 8 = 6k$ {{field-3}} {{field-4}}\n\nHence, we have that $3nmod6 =$ {{field-5}}.\n\nHowever, substituting $n = 0, 1, \u2026, 5$ into the expression $3n$, we obtain that\n$1, 2, 5$ {{field-6}}\nBut this is a contradiction since $3nmod6 =$ {{field-7}} by assumption."
